Providing Information to the Branch
You must be forthright in providing information to the Branch. Making a misleading statement or failing to
disclose a material fact (such as misstating information about the size of an event, or that the lease on your
property is about to run out, etc.) are contraventions.

A licensee must keep the following records, as applicable, for a period of at least six years from the date the
records were created:

a. liquor purchase records;
b. liquor sales records, including quantity of liquor sold and prices charged;
c. liquor disposal records;
d. food sales records;
e. sales records respecting other goods sold or services provided by the licensee in the establishment;
f. contracts with other licensees;
g. invoices and purchase receipts for all equipment and other inventory that is used in the operation of the
