The following designated liquor categories are recognized for the purposes of this exemption:

• draught beer;
• draught cider;
• beer served in bottle or cans;
• cider or coolers made with wine or spirits, served in bottles or cans;
• wine, other than wine coolers; and
• spirits, other than spirit coolers.

In such arrangements, the remaining minimum 10% of sales in a designated liquor category must come from
product/s supplied by a different supplier/s not associated with the exempted supplier, and may not be subject to
this type of financial arrangement. The availability of the liquor products that make up the remaining minimum
10% of sales must be made known to patrons at liquor sales locations within the stadium or concert hall.

